N5008 [expr.typeid]/1: the type_info key for a class type is its own
identity (tag), not a structural spelling of its components: a class with
member templates has method components whose parameter types are still
template parameters, which made the structural spelling throw and dropped
every body containing typeid(T) for such T (libstdc++'s
_Function_handler::_M_manager over a std::_Bind functor).
